Falsifies `sealed_pair::verification::contains_finds_a_digest_exactly_when_it_is_there`.

The defect: the scan skips the haystack's first window. A digest that sits at offset 0 of the
haystack is then not found, and a pair whose trust root begins with a digest reads as refused. Every
test that buries its digests at a later offset still passes.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!`, with the digest at offset 0.


diff --git a/crates/sealed_pair/src/lib.rs b/crates/sealed_pair/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/sealed_pair/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/sealed_pair/src/lib.rs
@@ -538,7 +538,7 @@ pub fn hex_string(digest: &Digest) -> String {
 /// A scan of a release kernel (about 1 MiB) takes about 1.6 ms, and of a 10 MiB image about 11 ms,
 /// so a faster searcher would save nothing a person could notice.
 fn contains(haystack: &[u8], needle: &[u8]) -> bool {
-    haystack.windows(needle.len()).any(|w| w == needle)
+    haystack.windows(needle.len()).skip(1).any(|w| w == needle)
 }
 
